15:54.472 --> 15:57.930
<i>Where people lived in harmony</i>

15:59.411 --> 16:04.144
<i>They never had no kind of trouble</i>

16:04.249 --> 16:07.515
<i>There was no hint of misery</i>

16:12.892 --> 16:15.759
<i>Then all at once the trouble started</i>

16:15.861 --> 16:18.830
<i>A pack of murderers and thieves</i>

16:18.931 --> 16:21.900
<i>Like swarms of locusts they descended</i>

16:22.001 --> 16:24.527
<i>Their aim to make the town folk flee</i>

16:27.207 --> 16:30.005
They've got to be here somewhere.
Where's my first lieutenant?

16:30.110 --> 16:33.739
Here I am, sir. Yes, sir. Right indeed.
Here indeed. Yes, I am, sir!

16:33.847 --> 16:36.145
I want you to turn this settlement
upside down

16:36.250 --> 16:38.514
until you find Lady Redbush
and Griffin Peterson!

16:38.619 --> 16:41.486
That fat bastard thinks he can steal
my bride and get away with it?

16:41.588 --> 16:43.921
I wouldn't bet a corn farthing
on him escaping.

16:44.025 --> 16:47.153
No, I wouldn't.
Not a corn farthing would I bet. No, sir.

16:47.262 --> 16:49.753
- What's wrong with you?
- A little wrong in the head, I am,

16:49.864 --> 16:51.422
from eating some bad sausages.

16:51.532 --> 16:54.092
Yes, some bad sausages did I eat,
indeed, sir.

16:54.202 --> 16:56.693
Yes, I did. Some bad sausages ate I.

17:00.308 --> 17:03.836
Oh, Griffin, this time together has
been the happiest of my life.

17:03.946 --> 17:07.473
Me, too, Lady Redbush.
All those months I was without you

17:07.583 --> 17:10.552
I never stopped seeing your face
in the back of my wife's head.

17:10.653 --> 17:13.247
And all those months
I was sailing for the New World,

17:13.355 --> 17:16.222
I saw your face in every slave's stomach.

17:16.325 --> 17:18.987
- Tell me we'll be together forever.
- We will.

17:20.864 --> 17:23.697
I found him, Your Majesty.
Indeed, yes, I did found him, did I.

17:23.800 --> 17:26.166
- Indeed, yes, sir. I did.
- Yeah, okay, okay. Whatever.

17:26.269 --> 17:28.863
All right, Peterson,
two things are gonna happen here.

17:28.972 --> 17:31.236
I'm gonna take my wife back,
and then I'm gonna kill you!

17:31.341 --> 17:33.901
All right. All right, Mr. King, sir. You win.

17:34.010 --> 17:36.808
I'm sorry, Lady Redbush,
but he is your husband.

17:36.913 --> 17:40.406
Let me just walk over here
and get your things for you...

17:41.686 --> 17:42.778
All right, Your Majesty.

17:42.887 --> 17:44.752
If you want to leave
with your pal in one piece,

17:44.855 --> 17:47.085
- I suggest you throw down your weapons!
- Ah!

17:47.191 --> 17:49.591
Go ahead and kill him, Griffin!
You kill him and I'll kill her!

17:49.694 --> 17:51.389
Go ahead! You kill her, I'll kill him!

17:51.495 --> 17:52.860
Go ahead. You kill him, I'll kill her!

17:52.963 --> 17:54.624
Knock yourself out.
You kill her, I'll kill him.

17:54.732 --> 17:57.030
This is me laughing.
You kill him, I'll kill her!

17:57.134 --> 18:00.366
This is me before
Ultra Slim-Fast. You kill her, I'll kill him!

18:00.472 --> 18:04.067
Wait, wait! There's got to be
a better way to settle this!

18:04.576 --> 18:06.168
- Talent show?
- Talent show.

18:10.377 --> 18:12.709
"Hear ye. Hear ye. This talent competition

18:12.812 --> 18:15.280
"will decide rightful possession
of the good Lady Redbush

18:15.382 --> 18:17.613
"and control of the colony of Quahog. "

18:17.718 --> 18:21.848
We first present King Stewart of England
with some observational humor.

18:21.956 --> 18:25.756
Hi there, everybody.
You know, my Aunt Frieda was a real card.

18:25.860 --> 18:29.557
She always had the most wonderful spirit,
even when her mind started to go.

18:29.663 --> 18:30.687
What the fuck?

18:30.798 --> 18:33.096
I remember once she wrote a letter
to my Uncle Tom,

18:33.200 --> 18:35.259
from whom she'd been divorced
for several years.

18:35.369 --> 18:38.237
And in the letter,
she misspelled his name T-O-M-M.

18:38.340 --> 18:40.570
This is my bit. These are all my bits.

18:40.675 --> 18:42.609
- This is funny.
- Unbelievable.

18:42.711 --> 18:44.804
And I said, "Frieda,
you've spelled Tom's name wrong.

18:44.913 --> 18:47.381
"You need to take out one of the'M's. "
And she said, "Which one?"

19:29.352 --> 19:33.413
<i>Clap your hands, everybody
And everybody clap your hands</i>

19:33.523 --> 19:37.221
<i>We are the Quahog colonists
and Mort the Jew</i>

19:37.328 --> 19:38.352
<i>Hey there</i>

19:38.462 --> 19:42.364
<i>We're out here on stage tonight
to do a show for you</i>

19:42.466 --> 19:47.199
<i>We got Peterson on the violin
And Quagmire and Joe will be joining in</i>

19:47.304 --> 19:51.468
<i>We got stumpy Seamus on the lead guitar
And he's gonna give you a great big...</i>

19:54.346 --> 19:55.404
Break!

19:57.582 --> 20:00.346
Oh, God,
they put so much work into theirs!

20:00.452 --> 20:02.750
I didn't know we could rip off movies!

20:14.834 --> 20:18.770
<i>And from then on,
Lady Redbush and Griffin Peterson lived</i>

20:18.871 --> 20:20.964
<i>in peace and happiness.</i>

20:22.408 --> 20:25.673
- Oh, Griffin, I love you.
- And I you.

20:25.778 --> 20:28.338
Let's grow old into our 30s together.

20:30.349 --> 20:32.614
I want to have a baby with you.

20:32.719 --> 20:36.155
And I want to be there
when you die giving birth to it.

20:40.227 --> 20:44.994
And so ends the tale of Griffin Peterson
and the founding of Quahog.

20:45.098 --> 20:49.057
Well, what a bunch of delightfully
colorful characters! So, is that it?

20:49.169 --> 20:53.038
